-- A default that supplies the input it would otherwise read reads nothing of it
-- (R8 rule 3, W7), even when that input's own default reads another input:
-- `k`'s default gives `h` its `b`, so `b`'s default, which reads `r`, is never
-- taken, and `r` is not read. It was refused as reading `r`
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7, §4.3, silent review S7).

§ `S`
    GIVEN r IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2
          b IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (r PLUS 1)

GIVETH A NUMBER
h MEANS b TIMES 10

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      k IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (h WITH b IS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
f MEANS x PLUS k

-- k is h with b given as 1, which is 10, whatever `r` is
#ASSERT (f WITH x IS 0) EQUALS 10
-- and a root that does not supply b still takes it from its r
#ASSERT h EQUALS 30
#ASSERT (h WITH r IS 5) EQUALS 60
